rammes until financing improves. That is the clearest sign that equity can't fund its capex. Pellham plans 2027 capex up 18% and is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- **Wider market:** Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size in Q3 2026. Equity appetite looks weak across the sector, not just for Pellham.\n- **Norvane Utilities:** It plans 2027 capex up 12%. It priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, so debt looks like its workable route. I found no evidence of a Norvane equity raise.\n- **Debt as the alternative:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Debt is more expensive but still open to at least some issuers.\n\n**Implication:** Expect capex to be cut or deferred, especially at Pellham, and for utilities to lean on debt where they can. That points to weaker grid-equipment demand in 2027.\n\n**Limits:** The evidence is thin. It comes from three documents (n5.d3, n5.d2, n2.d4). It has no equity valuation data and no figures on how much of the capex the utilities need equity to fund. Equity access could improve if markets recover.","ttft_ms":2173,"type":"result","duration_ms":24027,"uuid":"3371cc03-9298-4c68-907c-3035c50bf110","ttft_stream_ms":1016,"time_to_request_ms":70,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":3,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":20,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":60,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":202,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":128,"process_rss_mib_result":200,"process_anon_mib_result":120,"process_pea